1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,850
According to research studies coming out of top US universities, having high emotional intelligence, or EQ, can help you to succeed, particularly at work.
据美国顶尖大学的相关研究表明，拥有高情商（EQ）有助于个人取得成功，尤其是在工作领域。

2
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:31,270
The idea of emotional intelligence was introduced by psychologist John Mayer in the 90s and has gained popularity since, especially because it is said to be something that you can improve.
情商这一概念由心理学家约翰·迈尔于20世纪90年代提出，此后便逐渐受到广泛关注。这主要是因为，情商被认为是一种可以后天提升的能力。

3
00:00:31,270 --> 00:00:47,080
Someone with high emotional intelligence can supposedly build strong relationships, achieve their goals and manage their emotions – key areas for success in most jobs!
据称，高情商的人能够建立稳固的人际关系、实现个人目标并管理自身情绪，而这些都是大多数工作岗位中取得成功的关键要素。

4
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:53,460
It’s likely that, during your career, you will need to work in a team.
在你的职业生涯中，很可能需要参与团队协作。

5
00:00:53,460 --> 00:01:10,840
A 2020 Harvard study, published by the National Bureau of Economic Research, investigated social skills and team players. They did this by grouping volunteers and giving them a variety of tricky problems.
美国国家经济研究局于2020年发布了一项哈佛大学的研究，该研究围绕社交技能与团队合作者展开调查。

6
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:25,200
They then compared the top individual performers. Results showed two main reasons why these individuals excelled, both linked to emotional intelligence.
研究人员将志愿者分组，并为他们设置了一系列棘手的问题，随后对表现最为出色的个体进行了对比分析。

7
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:33,060
The first reason was that they were very good at recognising the emotional state of their teammates.
结果显示，这些佼佼者之所以脱颖而出，主要有两个原因，且均与情商密切相关。

8
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:40,270
The second was that they helped to improve their team’s performance through motivation.
第一，他们擅长识别队友的情绪状态；第二，他们通过激励的方式助力团队提升整体表现。

9
00:01:40,270 --> 00:01:53,850
When researching links between emotion-understanding ability and risk-taking, a 2012 Yale study found emotional intelligence to be critical to decision making.
耶鲁大学2012年在一项探究情绪理解能力与冒险行为关联性的研究中发现，情商对决策制定起着至关重要的作用。

10
00:01:53,850 --> 00:02:13,210
Researchers investigated the way that leaders come to a decision when they are under pressure. The results revealed that participants with a high awareness of why they felt under pressure managed to keep a clearer head and were less likely to take risks.
研究人员观察了领导者在面临压力时的决策方式，结果显示，那些能够清晰意识到自身压力来源的参与者，往往能保持头脑清醒，且更不容易做出冒险的决定。

11
00:02:13,210 --> 00:02:19,750
Being able to understand and manage emotions is a key part of EQ.
能够理解并管理情绪，是情商的核心组成部分。

12
00:02:19,750 --> 00:02:29,420
So, if you’re trying to succeed, work on your emotional intelligence and it may just make a difference!
因此，如果你渴望取得成功，不妨着力提升自己的情商——这或许会带来意想不到的改变。
